{"name":"Storksbill","hex":"#e5e1dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"storksbill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of genus Pelargonium.","Any plant of genus Erodium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storksbill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erodium","blocks":[{"text":"Erodium is a genus of flowering plants in the botanical family Geraniaceae. The genus includes about 120 species with a subcosmopolitan distribution, native to Europe, North Africa, Asia, Australia, and more locally in North and South America. They are perennials, annuals, or subshrubs, with five-petalled flowers in shades of white, pink, and purple, that strongly resemble the better-known Geranium (crane's-bills). In English-speaking areas of Europe, the species are known as stork's-bills. In North America they are known as filarees or heron's bill."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Erodium_January_2008-2.jpg/330px-Erodium_January_2008-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erodium"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG/500px-Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG/1280px-Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerbek_-_Le_Bec_de_cigogne_des_dunes_-_Storksbill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Erodium_lebelii_-_Dr%C3%BCsige_Hirtennadel_-_Kleverige_reigerb